<%# The page tree's column as this browser left it (`admin--shell--tree-width`
    remembers the chosen width in `localStorage`), said on <html> before
    anything is painted, the way the notes drawer's "open" is
    (`admin/shared/_notes_head`): the shell's grid reads
    `--admin-tree-width` (content-spiel.tailwind.css, 17rem without it), so
    the page is laid out at the chosen width from the first paint and the
    editor does not change width when the script connects. A value that is no
    number, or outside the two limits, is nobody's choice and sets nothing.

    `data-tree-fits` is the other thing the stylesheet cannot work out for
    itself: whether the tree, at that width, still fits BESIDE the notes
    column with the editor's least left (T3; a media query cannot read a
    custom property). It is said here for every screen, whether or not the
    notes are open or the screen has a tree: the stylesheet asks it only
    where both are so, and `admin--shell--tree-width` keeps it current from
    then on (a resized window, another width).

    THE UNIT IS THE STYLESHEET'S. The divider's figures
    (`Admin::Shell::TreeDividerComponent`) are pixels at a root font size of
    16px, and the stylesheet lays them out in rem, so each is multiplied here
    by the root's computed font size over 16, exactly as the controller does
    (its `scale`); only the notes column is pixels at any size. That is why
    this script is rendered AFTER the stylesheet's link and not before it as
    the other two head scripts are: a script waits for the stylesheets
    linked before it, so the font size it reads is the one the page is laid
    out with, whoever sets it (today nobody does: it is the browser's own).
    Still before <body> exists, so still before the first paint.

    Both stay on <html> for the life of the document: Turbo replaces <body>
    and merges <head>, never the root element, so a visit and Back find them
    as they were. Guarded like the theme's (`shared/_theme_head`):
    `localStorage` can throw, and the page is then laid out at the default. %>
<% divider = Admin::Shell::TreeDividerComponent %>
<%= javascript_tag nonce: true do %>
  (function () {
    var root = document.documentElement;
    var size = parseFloat(window.getComputedStyle(root).fontSize);
    var scale = size > 0 ? size / <%= divider::BASE %> : 1;
    var width = <%= divider::DEFAULT %> * scale;
    var stored = NaN;
    try { stored = parseFloat(localStorage.getItem("<%= divider::STORAGE_KEY %>")); } catch (e) {}
    if (stored >= <%= divider::MIN %> * scale && stored <= <%= divider::MAX %> * scale) {
      width = stored;
      root.style.setProperty("--admin-tree-width", stored + "px");
    }
    var sidebar = window.matchMedia("(min-width: 1280px)").matches ? <%= divider::SIDEBAR %> * scale : 0;
    if (window.innerWidth >= sidebar + width + <%= divider::NOTES %> + <%= divider::EDITOR %> * scale) root.setAttribute("data-tree-fits", "");
  })();
<% end %>
